## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Leaf project.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
1. `package.json` - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
3. `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component to root layout

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the Next.js 13.5+ installation method:

1. **Package Installation**: Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package using npm
   
2. **Component Integration**: 
   - Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
   - Added the component to the root layout body, alongside the existing `Analytics` component
   - This enables Speed Insights tracking across all pages in the application

3. **Framework-Specific Approach**: Used the Next.js App Router method as the project uses:
   - Next.js 16.2.9 (App Router architecture)
   - React 19.2.4
   - TypeScript

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully - no compilation errors
✅ Linting passed for modified files - no new errors introduced
✅ Package lock file updated correctly
✅ Existing code structure preserved - only added necessary imports and component

### Next Steps

To enable Speed Insights data collection:
1. Ensure Speed Insights is enabled in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. After deployment and user visits, Speed Insights metrics will be available in the project dashboard

### Notes

- The SpeedInsights component was placed right after the Analytics component in the layout body, following the existing pattern
- No breaking changes were introduced
- The implementation follows Next.js best practices for App Router layouts
